'' 'cptr( double ptr, @u )' stops dead at 'ptr' if the argument is parsed as an
'' expression, and the resulting FBX0401 desynchronises the parse badly enough to
'' swallow an 'end namespace' several hundred lines later. Which four intrinsics
'' accept a type was measured against fbc; TYPEOF is deliberately not among them,
'' because fbc does not accept it in expression position at all.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ast tests/parser/src/type-args.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: FBX0401
